      friendship: 0
  - title: Two signs
    number: 8
    heartsNeeded: 8
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - I've made two signs. Look. This one says 'Sterling Express'. They sent it, in the post, before I even said yes.
    - This one I painted myself last night. 'Kim's General Store. Local food, local people.' The paint isn't dry yet.
    - If I go local, you would have to bring me crops every week, and we would still be poor for a while. If I sign, we're safe, and it isn't ours any more.
    - You've been honest with me since the turnips. Be honest now. Which sign goes up?
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 1
      optionA: Go local
      replyA:
      - The wet one. Yes. The wet one.
      - Ji-ho, come down! Bring a ladder! And don't drop it on the slush machine this time!
      flagsA:
      - kims_local_supplier
      optionB: Take the franchise
      replyB:
      - Safe. Yes. Safe is good. My children won't have to do sums at midnight.
      - I'll ring them in the morning. You'll still come in, won't you? Even when it's... their shop?
      flagsB:
      - kims_franchise
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Sold out on Saturday
    number: 9
    heartsNeeded: 9
    path: 1
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - Saturday the whole 'From the farm' shelf was empty by eleven o'clock. Empty! I had to put up a sign saying 'More on Tuesday'.
    - People are coming back. Not everyone. But Grace Abara came in and said 'I'd rather pay a little more and know your name'.
    - Keep the crops coming, farmer. This shop has a future again, and half of it grows on your land.
    happy: 1
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 0
